// The rich-text flow seam (`setRichContent`), probed on its own.
//
// Flowed text is the one content kind whose LAYOUT the backend owns rather
// than the runtime: wrapping, block spacing, heading sizes and the code
// block's own shape are all decided on the far side of the seam. In an app
// that residual hides inside a much larger picture; alone on a dark field, a
// wrapping or leading disagreement is the whole frame.

App [ width = 400, height = 250, fill = #14181C, textColor = #E7EEF2,
    doc: Markdown [ x = 16, y = 12, width = 368, selectable = true,
        text = """
# Heading

A paragraph that must wrap at the flow's own measure, not the window's,
so a disagreement about the break point shows as a whole displaced line.

- a list item
- a second one

`inline code` beside ordinary prose.
""" ]
    ]
